# WebView Keyboard Handling

## Scaffold — CRITICAL

```dart
// ✅ CORRECT
resizeToAvoidBottomInset: false,

// ❌ WRONG — Flutter's Scaffold resize plus the JS scrollIntoView
// fire simultaneously and produce a visible jitter on every focus.
resizeToAvoidBottomInset: true,
```

`android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"` stays in `AndroidManifest.xml`.
The JS injection owns the keyboard inset — Flutter must NOT also consume it.

## JS keyboard mend

Called from `onPageFinished`. Constraints:

- `behavior: 'auto'` — NEVER `'smooth'`. A smooth scroll animation
  running concurrently with the IME opening causes a mid-animation
  snap-back.
- Single `setTimeout` at **350 ms** after `focusin`. Earlier (≤ 250 ms)
  runs before the IME finishes rendering; later (≥ 500 ms) feels
  sluggish.
- `visualViewport.resize` fallback at **120 ms** — catches Samsung /
  MIUI keyboards that don't fire `focusin`.
- Guard against non-editable elements (`INPUT`, `TEXTAREA`, or
  `isContentEditable === true`).

The concrete implementation lives in `_mendKeyboardScroll()` at
`lib/veil/web_veil.dart`. Do not rewrite this from scratch — audit
against the reference in `.cursor/rules/marble_pitfalls.md` §7.

## AndroidManifest.xml

```xml
android:windowSoftInputMode="adjustResize"
```

Do NOT change to `adjustPan` or `adjustNothing`. The former shifts the
whole window including the status-bar area; the latter kills the
inset entirely.
